+# Keep pickup reminders on SMS
+
+For volunteers considering a cheaper pickup reminder channel. Keep SMS because the email trial increased missed
+pickups and wasted fresh food; switching back to SMS restored the earlier missed-pickup rate.
+
+## Context
+
+Volunteers repeatedly proposed replacing SMS pickup reminders with email to save the reported €40 a month SMS
+cost. By [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), this was the third proposal that year.
+
+The pantry had already tried email reminders from April through June 2025. The discussion reports that the
+provider recorded 34% of reminder emails as never opened, while missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry
+orders. Each missed pickup leaves a packed bag; its fresh food goes in the bin by closing time. The pantry lead
+explained that many members share one phone in the family and never check email, but see SMS.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. In issue 52, the maintainer
+confirmed the decision to keep SMS. Reaching members and avoiding missed pickups and food waste therefore matter
+more than eliminating the reminder sending cost.
+
+## Options
+
+- **Email reminders**: free to send, saving the reported €40 monthly SMS bill. Rejected because the trial left
+  many reminders unopened and missed pickups rose to 13%, wasting the fresh food packed for those pantry orders.
+- **SMS reminders**: retain the sending cost, but reach members who do not check email. Chosen because missed
+  pickups returned to 6% after SMS resumed.
+
+## Decision
+
+Keep pickup reminders on SMS: the observed reduction in missed pickups and fresh food waste justifies the sending
+cost over email. The current channel is selected in [the reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py).
+
+## Consequences
+
+The pantry continues paying for SMS, reported as €40 a month in issue 52. The observed missed-pickup rate after
+returning to SMS was 6%, so reminders reduce missed pickups without eliminating them. Future proposals to save the
+SMS cost need to account for the email trial's effect on member reach, missed pickups and wasted fresh food.
